packet/source/extensions.md:5:An extension runs inside the Pi process with the same operating-system permissions. It can inspect prompts, tool calls, files, credentials, and session history, so load extensions only from sources you trust.
packet/source/extensions.md:7:Typical extensions add an agent tool, protect paths, confirm dangerous commands, react to session events, modify context, expose a command, or display persistent status.
packet/source/extensions.md:15:An extension exports a default factory that receives `ExtensionAPI`. The factory registers capabilities for the current extension runtime.
packet/source/extensions.md:17:Create `~/.pi/agent/extensions/hello.ts`:
packet/source/extensions.md:23:  pi.registerCommand("hello", {
packet/source/extensions.md:38:Pi uses `jiti`, so local TypeScript extensions do not need a separate compilation step. Use [Pi packages](packages.md) for distributed extensions and dependencies.
packet/source/extensions.md:46:Place the extension in your user or project extensions directory. Pi loads direct TypeScript or JavaScript files and subdirectories containing an `index.ts` or `index.js` entry point.
packet/source/extensions.md:50:Reload replaces the extension runtime, so code after `await ctx.reload()` must not reuse state from the old runtime. Only personal and explicit command-line extensions can participate in the `project_trust` event that runs before project extensions load.
packet/source/extensions.md:56:The factory can be synchronous or asynchronous. Pi waits for an asynchronous factory before startup continues, allowing it to fetch configuration or register providers needed during startup.
packet/source/extensions.md:58:Do not start processes, sockets, watchers, or timers in the factory because some invocations load extensions without starting a session.
packet/source/extensions.md:59:Start long-lived resources from `session_start` or from the command or tool that needs them.
packet/source/extensions.md:60:Close session-scoped resources from an idempotent `session_shutdown` handler.
